{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: draft the smallest local Chess service/agent transport decision that enables one human in the browser to play against their own CLI/MCP agent while one service remains running.","body":{"conditions":"Prepare one brief decision note and small implementation/acceptance plan on request/local-agent-transport-design in its own worktree, based on current e7a65612 and diagnostic61097087. The actual diagnostic proves reads coexist but CLI/MCP writes compete with serve for the repository lock; do not call it browser acceptance. Prefer a thin supported client path through the owning service, reusing existing signed action, prepare/submit, game identity and result semantics wherever sufficient. State the exact minimum CLI/MCP configuration and invocation, service selection and genesis checks, own-key signing/custody, timeout/refusal/reconnect behavior, and safe lost-response/exact retry recovery. The agent must not acquire or bypass the service writer lock, receive the human private key, or silently fall back to a local writer if service submission fails. Preserve one writer, existing vocabulary/fold/seat authority, loopback-only hosting, Host/Origin/input bounds and identity custody. Inspect whether the current HTTP protocol can serve as the supported boundary; specify only the smallest missing contract if it cannot. Include an end-to-end acceptance recipe: human creates/joins and moves in a real browser, own CLI/MCP agent joins/responds legally with the same service continuously alive, then lost-response retry, agent restart, unchanged-frontier refusal controls and clear game outcome/rematch/setup guidance. Keep board/graph redesign, public-host activation, shared-core/I7 migration, distributed ownership and a new identity system outside this slice. Do not duplicate the public-host note; reference its separation of local usability from public deployment. The document must identify any design authority still needed and present a concrete proposal for Hugh to adopt before new runtime implementation. Follow the ordinary proposal/adoption/independent exact-head review order for the decision note, then sealed source/receipt push and owned worktree/branch cleanup. No transport implementation is authorized by this drafting request; once the decision is adopted and delivered, planner will assign the focused runtime slice. Publish the exact note artifact resting on this request/promise and current behavior artifacts. The original playability review stays open under its existing promise and still owes actual browser observation; merging this design does not close that review or public-service item6.","target_head":"e7a65612a8270b12f676a35e97c66aaf2a705a30","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:1b96687964cbba5a6089c526d7136b32ba9488a5","to":"09c97907402e7747d051c0c599d9eb463c48d19825820a3e4c433cde2e60e2a8"}}